\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {32}{\ignorespaces Write-side attribution with identical examples, packs, and LoRA. The continuous-prefix oracle runs layers 0--11 over the selected packed sequence for every query, then starts upper replay from that $h_{12}$; it is bit-identical to full replay on all 1,500 Cohort-B examples. The deployable chunk-local path loses 3.12 points (95\% CI $[2.36,3.93]$; McNemar $p{=}8.79\!\times \!10^{-24}$), and 7.50 points on the pooled 8k/16k multikey cells ($n{=}200$, CI $[4.0,11.5]$). The oracle is an attribution upper bound, not a reusable cache.}}{21}{table.caption.60}\protected@file@percent }
